##Verification

- Tested all four input combinations for the AND logic.
- Tested a single injected fault in each of the three modules.
- Added a two-fault test to demonstrate the limitation of majority voting.
- A single faulty module is masked, while two faulty modules can cause an incorrect output.

##Limitations

- The design tolerates a single faulty module under the tested conditions.
- Two simultaneous faults can cause an incorrect output.
- The design masks faults but does not physically repair a faulty module.

